 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-187", "title": "spec align treats ch:trace marker literals inside test/fixture data as claimed markers, so a benign diff yields fail findings and exit 1", "detail": {"metadata": {}, "fingerprint": "0ec0abcf494bf7d0831e1d97615d081efb53e082c535e1850ad2b468ebefe2a1"}, "priority": "P3", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-18 during the goal check: _spec_check_markers scans every ADDED line for SPEC_TRACE_MARKER_RE and accepts a key=value run inside a python string literal as a claimed marker. tests/test_spec_ingest.py:233 supplies \"cite it as ch:trace row=X spec=docs/SPEC-001-graph.md\" as INPUT to the ingest converter (which then escapes it to ch&#58;trace), so any diff touching that line reports trace-missing-field/exit 1 for a change that violates nothing. AUG-153 (align guard enabled in no repo) is what makes this matter: the moment a repo enables the guard, such a diff blocks.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "AC1 PRE-FIX FALSIFIER (measured 2026-11-18 on 6f024c2): a diff whose only added line is a python test string containing \"ch:trace row=X spec=docs/SPEC-001-graph.md\" makes `python3 auger.py spec align --repo-root . --spec-root specs --protocol-version 1 --diff-file /tmp/aug187.diff` print a finding with code=trace-missing-field and exit 1 (reproduced with the 82395-byte 3e1ffd0..HEAD diff and with a one-line test-fixture addition).\nAC2 PREFERRED FIX: on that same diff the verb exits 0 and emits no finding of severity=fail, because a key=value run that sits inside a string literal (or that follows non-trailer prose) is no longer read as a claimed marker; the exit code and the full finding set are captured in the closeout evidence.\nAC3 ACCEPTABLE ALTERNATIVE: the constraint is made explicit instead — docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md states that marker EXAMPLES in test or fixture data must be written escaped (ch&#58;trace), and tests/test_spec_alignment_check.py pins both directions (escaped example -> no fail; bare marker line -> still trace-missing-field).\nAC4 NON-VACUITY: a diff that adds a real bare marker line `ch:trace row=AUG-187` without commit= still yields code=trace-missing-field and exit 1, so whichever resolution lands keeps the mandatory-field rule at full strength.\nAC5 GATE ARM: any new or amended test file is named in the tests/gate.sh line-218 pytest arm and `grep -c test_spec_alignment_check tests/gate.sh` is >= 1.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-18T01:16:50Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-18T14:35:09Z", "foreman_note": "COS card manager 2026-11-18: unfiled-linkage + gate repair note. (1) This row cites no initiative card in its reasoning; the COS has attached it to kanban card t_d7ac1156 ([auger] Docs/spec parity + GitReins spec_alignment wiring) as of this pass. (2) It FAILS the dispatchability gate on unexpanded placeholders <diff>/<that file>; AUG-184 owns the mechanical repair — rewrite against the literal fixture tests/test_spec_ingest.py:233 and the real verb (auger spec align --repo /home/kara/auger) so a worker needs no context.\n\nPM PASS7 2026-11-20T10:56:53Z (tick auger-pm-2026-11-20-09-16-17): dispatchability repair — AC1 now names the literal diff file the probe writes (/tmp/aug187.diff, produced by git diff 3e1ffd0..HEAD) and AC5 names the real gate-arm file tests/test_spec_alignment_check.py. Criteria intent unchanged; no status/priority/commit_hash/evidence field moved. Live gate after repair: acceptance_gate.py audit reports this row passing.", "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null, "type": "bug"}
